tube; the profiles are its Table over the radius"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"838d0c8b-b131-49a8-afc5-8808252e7df6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A region on a graph is measured by counting vertices, and its boundary is \
not negligible at a finite scale: the vertices at distance exactly ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ffb34cb-ad3a-49ce-94db-1f824a75cd26"],
 " are a share of order ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", "/", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "bb7957a2-a8ea-4c0e-b39a-c5fc878885bd"],
 " of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51401111-b0bc-4109-8159-33fe2e818c57"],
 ". So every region carries two measures. The counting measure is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["A", "TI"]},
    "Abs"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0be170dd-fd36-4ba5-b756-a94d569ecf38"],
 ". The Riemannian measure is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"], 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}]}], "=", 
   TemplateBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"]},
    "Abs"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69778435-a2e2-4f03-acfb-3244863ee1aa"],
 ", where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[SmallCircle]"], "=", "{", 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], ":", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[SubsetEqual]", 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "d640df2c-04ab-4b83-987a-d79bc40fe1e1"],
 " is the set of vertices all of whose neighbours lie in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "44b9af0c-3b37-4271-9ac3-e76524795121"],
 "; it is the count without the boundary and the default of the growth \
estimators."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"61fb641e-e0af-494f-b4db-8cd42ea2b21e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the square grid the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["r", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a3773796-ba40-47fe-a472-1fcf3ba18e47"],
 " has counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "+", "2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "990be4aa-963e-44fa-9010-c0cbd8b50556"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["r", "TI"], "2"], "-", "2", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "+", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64196ad2-36f4-4a13-a615-8c29cf5611df"],
 ", the counting measure of the ball of radius ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["r", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8c215b5b-3174-4c12-a741-1acd1334af50"],
 "; the shell has counting measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", 
   StyleBox["r", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8ab09190-f419-4e06-b2fa-bdc6c80df97b"],
 " and Riemannian measure ",
 Cell[BoxData["0"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a5c01c58-6f0d-45f3-8dea-24cedd60b6b3"],
 ". The same shift holds on the triangular lattice before the rim, the \
convention of the Wolfram Physics technical introduction."
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d356c562-6e44-45a2-8b4e-30a5f9cb694c"],

